# Plan Artifact Template

Use this as the full body template for the planning artifact.

```markdown
<!-- AI_SIMPLE_PLAN:START -->
# PLAN::ISSUE-ID

## Source Request
- Tracker: `{{ workflow_tracker }}`
- Issue / task id: `ISSUE-ID`
- Title: `...`
- Source contract: present / missing / partial
- Notes: prerequisites, constraints, missing artifacts

## Implementation Decisions
Capture gray-area choices **before** the step plan (layouts, API shapes, error handling, data structures). Use `/clarify` when this section would be mostly `TBD`. Skip only for trivial, single-file changes.

- Decision 1: ...
- Decision 2: ...
- Defaults accepted (if any): ...

## Minimal Solution Ladder
{% if minimalism_enabled and minimalism_level != "off" -%}
Required when `minimalism.enabled` is true. Run **before** `File Map`. Each requirement must pick the highest working rung (1–6). `CREATE` entries need justification when rung < 6.

| Requirement | Rung (1–6) | Chosen approach | Skipped alternatives | ponytail-debt? |
|-------------|------------|-----------------|----------------------|----------------|
| ... | 3 native | `<input type="date">` | flatpickr wrapper | no |
| ... | 2 stdlib | `functools.lru_cache` | custom cache class | yes: global lock |

Intensity: `{{ minimalism_level }}` from `ai.config.yaml`. `change_class: small` → default `full`; `large` greenfield may use `lite` only when explicitly noted in `Implementation Decisions`.
{% else -%}
Optional. Skip when `minimalism.enabled` is false or `minimalism.level` is `off`.
{% endif -%}

## Execution Contract

```json
{
  "change_class": "small|medium|large",
  "risk_level": "low|medium|high",
  "system_shape": ["cli", "templates", "docs", "runtime-surfaces"],
  "owner_surfaces": ["src/...", "template/..."],
  "touches_docs": true,
  "touches_runtime_surfaces": true,
  "cross_profile": false
}
```

